    {
      "id": "be-s12m-shutdown-long-run-c1",
      "heading": "Losses and the shutdown rule",
      "explanation_md": "If Pe is below ATC, **Profit = (Pe - ATC) x Qf* < 0**: a loss.\n\nA firm should **keep operating** (sustain short-run losses) if its **operating loss is less than its fixed costs**, because operating loses less than shutting down.\n\n**Decision rule:**\n\n- **Shut down when P < min AVC.**\n- **Continue as long as P ≥ min AVC.**\n\nSo the firm's **short-run supply curve** is its **MC curve above minimum AVC**.",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Shut down if P < min AVC; supply curve = MC above min AVC.",
      "clarification": null,
