    {
      "id": "be-s12m-shutdown-long-run-c3",
      "heading": "Entry in the long run",
      "explanation_md": "With **barriers to entry**, price takers' profits **persist**. In **perfect competition** there is **free entry**, so:\n\n1. Short-run profits lead to **entry**.\n2. Entry **increases market supply**, **drives down the market price** and increases market quantity.\n3. Each firm's **demand shifts down**.\n4. The firm **reduces output**.\n5. **Long-run profits are zero.**\n\n**Long-run competitive equilibrium:**\n\n| Condition | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| P = MC | Socially efficient output |\n| P = minimum AC | Efficient plant size |\n| Zero profits | Firms earn just enough to offset their opportunity cost |",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Profits attract entry, price falls, profits go to zero; long run: P = MC = minimum AC.",
      "clarification": null,
      "check_questions": [
        {
          "id": "be-s12m-shutdown-long-run-q-163e3910",
