    {
      "id": "be-s12m-shutdown-long-run-q-7f689eb0",
      "type": "short",
      "stem": "Explain the shutdown decision rule for a perfectly competitive firm.",
      "options": [],
      "answer": "",
      "accept": [],
      "explanation": "",
      "model_answer_md": "When **Pe < ATC** the firm makes a loss: (Pe - ATC) x Qf* < 0. It should still **operate** if its **operating loss is less than its fixed costs**, since shutting down would lose all fixed costs.\n\n- **Shut down when P < min AVC.**\n- **Continue while P ≥ min AVC.**\n\nSo the short-run supply curve is **MC above minimum AVC**.",
